{"id":8195929,"docketId":65293714,"caseName":"Williams v. Miller","caseNameFull":"Williams v. Miller","slug":"williams-v-miller","docketNumber":"No. 492","dateFiled":"1942-12-07","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1942,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Mr. John L. McNab for appellants. Messrs. Earl Warren, Attorney General of California, and Lucas E. Kilkenny, Deputy Attorney General, for appellees.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":38,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8157864,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1021,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"ACX\">\n\n<em>Per Curiam:</em>\n</author>\n<p id=\"A3i\">The decree dismissing the bill of complaint is affirmed on the ground that the bill does not allege facts which would warrant the granting of equitable relief by a federal court to restrain enforcement of the state statute. <em>Spielman Motor Co. </em>v. <em>Dodge, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"102437\"><a href=\"/opinion/102437/spielman-motor-sales-co-v-dodge/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Spielman Motor Sales Co. v. Dodge\">295 U. S. 89</a></span>; <em>Beal </em>v. <em>Missouri Pacific R. Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"103437\"><a href=\"/opinion/103437/beal-v-missouri-pacific-r-corp/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Beal v. Missouri Pacific R. Corp.\">312 U. S. 45</a></span>; <em>Watson </em>v. <em>Buck, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"103535\"><a href=\"/opinion/103535/watson-v-buck/#400\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Watson v. Buck\">313 U. S. 387, 400-01</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}